WEBVTT

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:08.110
Hsinking, 1939

00:00:55.110 --> 00:01:01.120
<b>Asia                 Asia</b>

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:52.910
I'm bored...

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:55.510
Hey, let's do something.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.170
Like what?

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:58.400
Brother!

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:02.680
<b>The
Treasure Island 
Expedition</b>

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.130
What're you reading?

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:02.680
The Treasure Island Expedition.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:05.530
Let's go on an expedition!

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.140
I would, but...

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.390
You're not allowed to run off.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.100
Oh, yes.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.460
The obi on that kimono was just gorgeous.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:14.530
I'll say.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.300
Hey, can we go on an expedition?

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.050
Sit still and be quiet.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.140
But we're bored!

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.620
Hush. Be quiet!

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.290
<b>Wash Room</b>

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:10.960
<b>Wash Room</b>

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.550
<b>Men's Toilet</b>

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.120
<i>As the embers of world war smoldered</i>

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.410
<i>in autumn of 1937,</i>

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.720
<i>the Imperial Army</i>

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.000
<b>Greater East Asia 
Cultural Society</b>

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.920
<b>Greater East Asia 
Cultural Society</b>

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.920
<i>established a clandestine spy training agency.</i>

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:57.810
<i>The histories, names, and even ages</i>

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:00.980
<i>of the elite men who pass its 
rigorous application process</i>

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:04.090
<i>are all treated as top-secret information.</i>

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:07.870
<i>They easily complete training 
exercises that push them</i>

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.810
<i>to their physical and mental limits.</i>

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.730
<i>Under the command of founder 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki,</i>

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.810
<i>they operate worldwide, within the shadows.</i>

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:20.490
<i>And so a brand-new intelligence 
agency was created.</i>

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:23.950
<i>Its name is "D-Agency."</i>

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:01.880
Episode 6 - Asia Express

00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:58.340
<i>Anton Morozoff.</i>

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:03.120
<i>A second-class secretary working for the 
Soviet Union consulate in Manchuria.</i>

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:06.900
<i>About half a year ago,</i>

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:10.180
<i>we "burned" his history of lavishing money on</i>

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:11.700
<i>a Harbin nightclub girl.</i>

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:15.940
<i>Three days ago, Morozoff sent us</i>

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:20.060
<i>an emergency communication via a 
classified newspaper advertisement.</i>

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.170
<i>Given the large sum of money he requested,</i>

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:26.150
<i>we believed he had highly 
classified, top-secret info.</i>

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:33.870
This program is a work of fiction. 
The characters, organizations, locations, laws, names, 
etc. being portrayed are unrelated to actual events.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:29.930
<i>The information was to be printed</i>

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:31.780
<i>on the newspaper he'd be carrying.</i>

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:35.290
<i>We planned to make the trade 
after meeting in the wash room</i>

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.750
<i>and confirming each other's identities...</i>

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:51.430
<i>SMERSH...</i>

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.400
<i>Death to spies, huh?</i>

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:55.720
<i>The Hanged Man...</i>

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:59.330
<i>Judas, the man who betrayed Jesus Christ.</i>

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.580
<i>The secret organization that
mercilessly assassinates</i>

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:05.190
<i>traitors to the USSR.</i>

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:18.120
<b>Men's Toliet</b>

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:09.170
<i>In their minds, you either dedicate your life</i>

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:11.820
<i>to the revolution, or die.</i>

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:16.080
<i>Same as a certain group 
of zealots in the army</i>

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.880
<i>obsessed with the "military code."</i>

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:29.410
<i>Now that the assassin has the 
encoded newspaper message,</i>

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:31.510
<i>he'll likely get off next, at Mukden.</i>

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.350
<i>We arrive in...</i>

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:36.200
<i>A little over an hour.</i>

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:44.310
<i>From a timing standpoint,</i>

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:47.370
<i>it's most likely he met 
Morozoff in the wash room.</i>

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:48.690
<i>However,</i>

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:52.650
<i>Morozoff was fully aware that he was a traitor,</i>

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:55.160
<i>and feared being assassinated.</i>

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:01.640
<i>If that suspicious-looking fellow 
really was a SMERSH assassin,</i>

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:05.000
<i>Morozoff wouldn't have turned his 
back and left himself defenseless.</i>

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:11.420
<i>Did he do something to get 
Morozoff to drop his guard?</i>

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:17.140
<i>Or...</i>

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:23.470
Hey, mister, are you a magician?

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:26.130
Nope, this is just a little hobby of mine.

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:29.540
Can you do any other tricks?

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:30.530
I'm afraid not.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:32.130
Oh...

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.950
The tea was to die for...

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:38.400
Hey, mister, my brother's pretty amazing, too.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:41.350
He knows everything there 
is to know about the Asia.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:44.330
You don't have to tell him that. He doesn't care.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.880
Our dad works for the 
South Manchurian Railway,

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:51.090
so I know a little bit more 
than other kids. That's all.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.320
Oh, really?

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:54.130
Please, tell me about it.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:56.640
Well, for starters...

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:00.400
The Asia's top speed is 110 kilometers,

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:03.940
so it can travel the 704.1 
kilometers between Hsinking

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:01.720
<b>Hsinking</b>

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:04.810
<b>Mukden</b>

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:06.460
and Dairen in eight hours and twenty minutes.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.100
<b>Dairen</b>

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:08.480
Stuff like that?

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:11.480
Wow, he was right. You know a lot!

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:12.540
See?

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:18.220
The railway's last special express 
before the Asia was called the Pigeon,

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:20.500
but it was a bit slower than the Swallow,

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:23.400
which was the special express 
that ran between Tokyo and Kobe

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:25.280
on the Tokaido main line.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:29.430
Yeah, with the real birds, a swallow's 
a lot quicker than a pigeon, too.

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:33.410
So the South Manchurian Railway 
built this train, the Asia,

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:34.750
to beat the Swallow.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:37.650
It's faster 'cuz it's more streamlined!

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:42.350
The Asia's average speed 
is 84.2 kilometers per hour.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.520
It's the fastest train in the Orient!

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:45.830
Wow.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.030
You really know your stuff.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:50.410
Where are you boys disembarking?

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:51.810
Dairen.

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:54.480
We've got... six hours to go.

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:58.740
We got bored, so we're playing expedition.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:01.920
<i>Forty-five minutes until we reach Mukden.</i>

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:07.330
Okay, boys, now I've got a riddle for you.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:12.420
If I got off at the stop in Mukden,

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:16.230
how could I send a letter to
the final destination, Dairen,

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:17.830
faster than the Asia?

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:20.310
Mister, weren't you listening?

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:23.290
The Asia's the fastest train in all the Orient!

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:25.840
Nothing can get there faster than the Asia.

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:28.430
You dope! Think about it a little.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:29.700
Huh?

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:32.100
I know! An airplane!

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:34.410
Where are you gonna find an airplane?

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:36.580
You couldn't get to the airfield fast enough.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:37.990
Oh, yeah...

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:42.490
I give up. How?

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:48.650
I've got a mission for your expedition.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:50.380
A mission?

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:52.960
Today is July 25th.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:56.660
Your mission is to find a 
person reading a newspaper

00:10:56.950 --> 00:11:00.300
from the 24th, or the 23rd... 
one that's a few days old,

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:01.800
and secretly drop

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:05.760
this tarot card at his feet.

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:09.700
Once you drop the card, 
come straight back to me.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:11.040
Understand?

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:16.670
He's in the third-class passenger 
cabin in front of this one.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:20.700
When you come back, tell me 
what clothes he was wearing.

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:24.000
Once you complete your mission safely,

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:26.660
I'll tell you the answer.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:29.820
We're not supposed to wander off, though...

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:34.630
Don't worry. We'll just say 
we're going to the bathroom.

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:39.880
<i>The newspaper</i>

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:43.250
<i>containing the encoded information</i>

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:45.680
<i>was marked up with a special invisible ink.</i>

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:49.240
<i>A task too involved for a novice</i>

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:53.230
<i>like Morozoff to be able to 
pull off using today's paper.</i>

00:11:55.350 --> 00:11:58.940
<i>He probably used one from a few days ago.</i>

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:35.560
Brother, wait!

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:02.510
We found him!

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:07.280
He was in the third-class 
passenger cabin in car four.

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:08.910
We dropped the card, too.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:09.930
Great job.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:11.470
You remember what he was wearing?

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:12.350
A white...

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:14.510
A white jacket and black pants!

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:17.940
The lining of his jacket was black, too.

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:19.430
Thanks.

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:21.460
You boys make great scouts.

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:23.400
Can I buy you some drinks?

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:24.710
Really?

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.620
Hmm...

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.050
Tea is ready. 
Dining Car Service 
is available

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.660
I want lemonade.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:36.830
What are you doing?!

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:39.900
I'm terribly sorry.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:42.110
No, no, please don't be.

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:46.550
I was a bit bored myself, so the 
boys and I have been conversing.

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:48.960
Come on, back to your seats.

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:53.260
Aw, but he was about to tell us 
the answer to the riddle!

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:56.200
I promise I'll tell you later.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.880
For now, you'd better do as your mother says.

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:00.950
Okay...

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:10.110
<i>Twenty minutes to go.</i>

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:25.290
We'll be arriving in Mukden shortly.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:29.590
Departing passengers, please take 
care not to leave anything behind.

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:35.450
Ladies and gentlemen, for your own safety,

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:38.810
please stay seated until the 
train comes to a complete stop.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:45.710
We'll be arriving in Mukden shortly.

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:48.300
Departing passengers, please take care

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:50.120
not to leave anything behind.

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:57.540
Excuse me. We'll be arriving in Mukden shortly.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:03.080
Don't come out. Just listen.

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:06.080
The enemy's aware of our identity.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:08.880
But he doesn't yet suspect the conductor, me—

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:33.320
How... did you...

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:37.110
Morozoff feared assassination,
 so it had to be someone

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:39.540
who could sneak up without arousing suspicion.

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.750
Someone like a conductor.

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:46.660
Relax. Unlike you, I'm not a killer.

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:48.560
Have a good sleep.

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:52.600
Damn you...

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:03.390
It's over,

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:05.100
Miss Elena.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:05.980
<b>Elena</b>

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:14.160
Anton Morozoff wasn't alone.

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:17.580
You were fleeing the country 
with him, weren't you?

00:16:20.940 --> 00:16:23.270
It's all set. No problem.

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:25.650
This info's worth a lot of money.

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:29.930
We'll escape to Japan, 
and from there, America.

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:36.640
<b>Wash Room</b>

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:34.770
Come, let's get back to our room.

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:39.100
Pardon me.

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:43.840
The assassin, who'd realized I was on board,

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.550
needed to buy time to kill Morozoff

00:16:46.550 --> 00:16:48.310
and dispose of the evidence.

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:54.790
So you deliberately stood in front of 
your room, blocking the path between

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:58.700
the first-class cabin and the corridor 
to buy him the time he needed.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:12.960
<b>Luggage</b>

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:12.960
<b>Ladies' Toilet</b>

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:11.550
In other words,

00:17:11.850 --> 00:17:14.550
you were in cahoots with the assassin.

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:19.570
They threatened me...

00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:23.940
No, you chose to sell him out.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:28.090
You never had any intention 
of going to America.

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:35.740
Don't worry.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:38.950
I'm not planning to turn you over to SMERSH.

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:43.970
But...

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:49.420
I expect you'll have to go to work for Japan.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:33.250
The one thing faster than 
the Asia is the pigeon.

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:34.610
Huh?!

00:18:34.610 --> 00:18:36.750
That's not the answer!

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:39.720
Even the Swallow is faster than the Pigeon!

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:44.000
And the Asia's speed of 80 kilos 
per hour beats the Swallow!

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:46.740
There are different kinds of pigeons out there.

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:47.740
Here...

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:49.440
Just watch.

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:01.450
<i>Manchuria is a scheming country.</i>

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:04.640
<i>All the telegraph communication 
lines are monitored.</i>

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:07.910
<i>One has to assume their messages 
are getting intercepted.</i>

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:10.000
<b>Hsinking</b>

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:16.750
<b>Mukden</b>

00:19:09.590 --> 00:19:12.730
<i>To guarantee both of our safety,</i>

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:15.500
<i>I needed a way to contact 
the D-Agency agent waiting</i>

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:19.490
<i>at the end of the line in Dairen 
that was even faster than the Asia.</i>

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:19.070
<b>Dairen</b>

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:21.910
<i>With a tailwind,</i>

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.930
<i>a carrier pigeon's speed can
top 100 kilometers per hour.</i>

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:27.590
<i>With the winds at this time of year,</i>

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:31.680
<i>I calculated that a carrier pigeon 
could reach Dairen faster.</i>

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:37.550
<i>We learned details of the Soviet Union's 
next moves from Morozoff's info.</i>

00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:39.670
<i>It turned out to be extremely valuable.</i>

00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:43.890
<i>But the real problems start now 
that D-Agency has that intel.</i>

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:49.120
<i>Lately, I feel that the information 
we're working so hard to obtain</i>

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:51.290
<i>isn't being applied effectively.</i>

00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:56.190
<i>Using the info is harder than obtaining it.</i>

00:19:56.980 --> 00:19:59.680
<i>Against the hardheads of the 
Imperial Army's top brass,</i>

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:02.640
<i>no matter how hard 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki fights,</i>

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:05.550
<i>there's not much more we can accomplish.</i>

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:09.640
<i>Spies can only be effective in peacetime.</i>

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:12.300
<i>Once a war starts,</i>

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:15.030
<i>the meaning of our existence vanishes.</i>

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:21.650
<i>Oh, well.</i>

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:24.620
<i>All I can do is do what I can.</i>

00:22:18.780 --> 00:22:22.400
About the Soviet spy detained in Manchuria...

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:25.070
The intelligence made its 
way to D-Agency's hands.

00:22:25.590 --> 00:22:27.980
And they let him leave with his life.

00:22:28.500 --> 00:22:32.030
"Don't die, don't kill..." Them again?

00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:35.040
They're like a rotten apple!

00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:37.640
They're certain to have a negative influence

00:22:37.640 --> 00:22:40.620
on the great Imperial Japanese Army.

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:41.990
Come on,

00:22:42.350 --> 00:22:46.500
it's not such a big deal having 
an intelligence agency

00:22:46.500 --> 00:22:48.720
acting in service to the Imperial Army's code.

00:22:49.030 --> 00:22:51.900
Then they've given the approval?

00:22:52.730 --> 00:22:53.600
Yes...

00:22:54.520 --> 00:22:58.530
It's about time we had the 
D-Agency boys make their exit.

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:23.330
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:20.770 --> 00:23:23.330
Wasn't there an artist who compared 
life to an ocean voyage?

00:23:23.650 --> 00:23:27.590
You start rowing from a small stream, 
enjoy the peaceful scenery,

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:29.760
